    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNo. 33 Pallas Derg, Newtown, is an immaculately presented 3-bedroom end-of-terrace home, ideally positioned at the end of a quiet cul-de-sac within this highly desirable residential development of just 42 homes.\n\nNewtown is a popular village located approximately 8 km from Nenagh town and close to the shores of Lough Derg. The village offers an excellent range of local amenities including a national school, church, pub/restaurant, créche, coffee dock, GAA and soccer clubs, making it an attractive location for families, first-time buyers and those looking to enjoy village living.\n\nThe property itself is an exceptional home, boasting an impressive garden with a particularly large side garden, providing an abundance of outdoor space rarely found with a property of this type.\n\nInternally, the house has been beautifully maintained and presented. The spacious living room features solid oak flooring and a solid fuel inset stove with granite surround, creating a warm and inviting space. The solid oak flooring continues throughout the ground floor, with the exception of the kitchen area which is fully tiled.\n\nThe dining area is a particular feature of the home, with a vaulted ceiling and French doors opening directly onto the rear garden. Outside, a new artificial grass area has been installed, providing a practical, low-maintenance space for year-round use, while the generous side garden remains laid in lawn.\n\nUpstairs, there are three well-proportioned bedrooms, including two large double bedrooms with built-in wardrobes and a spacious single bedroom. The accommodation is completed by a fully tiled family bathroom.\n\nThis exceptional property would make an ideal first-time buyer home, family residence or retirement property, offering generous accommodation, excellent outdoor space and a highly desirable village location.\n\nViewing is strictly by appointment and is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 1.858m x 5.532d\nSolid Oak floor\n\nLiving Room - 3.643w x 5.512d\nSolid Oak floor, solid fuel inset stove with granite surround\n\nW.C. - 1.289w x 1.1d\n\n\nKitchen - 3.132 x 3.354d\nTiled, Integrated Hob, Oven and dishwasher.Granite worktops\n\nDining Area - 2.439w x 6.308d\nSolid Oak floor, Vaulted ceiling, french doors to rear\n\nBathroom - 2.32w x 2.08d\nFully tiled, electric shower.\n\nMaster Bedroom - 3.56 w x 3.995d\nTimber floor 8 door built in wardrobe\n\nBedroom 2 - 2.86w x 4.87d\nTimber floor, built in wardrobe\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.66w x 3d\nTimber floor, built in wardrobe\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Immaculate interior finish.</li><li> Sandstone facade.</li><li> Exceptionally large side garden ideal for families or enjoying outdoor space.</li><li> Located in popular village location with good National School.</li><li> Open fire in living room with solid fuel inset stove and granite surround.</li><li> Vaulted ceiling in dining room with access to rear garden.</ul>"
